            <title>[LU-20565] FLR-EC: reduce sanity-ec.sh subtests to use minimum OSTCOUNT possible </title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20565</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The current sanity-ec.sh subtests often require 6 or 8 OSTs in order to run.  However, much of the functionality could be adequately tested with &lt;tt&gt;&amp;#45;&amp;#45;ec 2+1&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;&amp;#45;&amp;#45;ec 2+2&lt;/tt&gt; if &lt;tt&gt;OSTCOUNT&lt;/tt&gt; was 3 or 4.  Otherwise, the majority of the sanity-ec.sh subtests are skipped in Janitor testing and we lose important and timely test coverage on patches.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
